Armor, weapons and various useful items in Nethack are not impervious to 
damage without mystical means.

Yet when one comes upon such an item in the mines whether it's brand 
spanking new and fresh from Ms. Wonotobo's shop or a cursed, rusted-out and 
thoroughly corroded item found on some poor soul's bones the item looks the 
same.

Items that reach their limit on one form of ablation (corrosion, rust, rot, 
burnt, etc...) would no longer be brown or a steely blue. A thoroughly 
burnt or rotted pair of leather gloves would now be black (like a 
carnivorous ape, I'm not advocating invisibility) and thoroughly corroded 
bronze plate mail would take on a greenish patina (like some helmets) when 
found on the floor. Iron or steel items would become an orange-red 
(#CC6600) to represent the corrosion.


